# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: hz-06-the-second-shove
number: 206
name: The Second Shove
description: Walls and pits set one tile apart. The first shove only staggers; the Stagger is what makes the second one lethal, and it expires at end of round.
design: Hazard Pressure 6 of 10 — the chain.
design: Three L-shaped cells: a wall on one axis, a pit one tile away on the other. Shove into the wall for 4 and a Stagger; the Stagger makes the NEXT displacement travel one tile further, which is exactly the tile that beats a Footing token. Stagger clears at end of round, so both halves of the chain have to happen inside one round, with two different units.
design: No high ground here on purpose: this fight is entirely about the horizontal.

spawn g = Grappler
spawn l = Lobber
spawn s = Stalker
spawn h = Husk

footing: enemy=1

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..g..lB
  ..#.#.B
  .O...OB
  .......
  .^...O.
  A...#^.
  AA.s.h.
